"use strict";(self.webpackChunkspa_template=self.webpackChunkspa_template||[]).push([[391],{9391:s=>{s.exports=JSON.parse('{"created":"2017-04-26T14:29:00","modified":"2017-04-26T14:29:00","id":1033,"title":"React JSX - Remember What It Compiles Too","article":"<p>Be careful of your children :)</p>\\n<p>When creating components its important to remember that JSX compiles to something else. This article talks about a specific example, but it is important to keep in mind what the output is when developing anything.</p>\\n<p>I was creating a Loader component, that either displayed an icon or its children depending a flag, when I had made it though I realised I should not be using children like that as it is poorly performing.</p>\\n<h2 id=\\"whats-the-problem\\">Whats the problem?</h2>\\n<p>Fig 1 shows the Loader in use and Fig 2 shows the compiled the output from <a href=\\"https://babeljs.io/repl/\\">Babel Repl</a>. Remember the Loader component doesn’t actually use the children unless completed is true, however as we can see in Fig 2 all of the children run the React.createElement function regardless, only being excluded in the render method of Loader. </p>\\n<h3 id=\\"fig-1---original\\">Fig 1 - Original</h3>\\n<pre><code class=\\"hljs language-js\\"><span class=\\"hljs-keyword\\">const</span> isComplete = <span class=\\"hljs-literal\\">true</span>;\\n\\n<span class=\\"hljs-function\\"><span class=\\"hljs-keyword\\">function</span> <span class=\\"hljs-title\\">App</span>(<span class=\\"hljs-params\\"></span>) </span>{\\n    <span class=\\"hljs-keyword\\">return</span> (\\n        <span class=\\"xml\\"><span class=\\"hljs-tag\\">&lt;<span class=\\"hljs-name\\">Loader</span> <span class=\\"hljs-attr\\">completed</span>=<span class=\\"hljs-string\\">{isComplete}</span>&gt;</span>\\n            <span class=\\"hljs-tag\\">&lt;<span class=\\"hljs-name\\">ul</span>&gt;</span>\\n              <span class=\\"hljs-tag\\">&lt;<span class=\\"hljs-name\\">li</span>&gt;</span>A<span class=\\"hljs-tag\\">&lt;/<span class=\\"hljs-name\\">li</span>&gt;</span>\\n              <span class=\\"hljs-tag\\">&lt;<span class=\\"hljs-name\\">li</span>&gt;</span>B<span class=\\"hljs-tag\\">&lt;/<span class=\\"hljs-name\\">li</span>&gt;</span>\\n            <span class=\\"hljs-tag\\">&lt;/<span class=\\"hljs-name\\">ul</span>&gt;</span>\\n            <span class=\\"hljs-tag\\">&lt;<span class=\\"hljs-name\\">div</span>&gt;</span>\\n              <span class=\\"hljs-tag\\">&lt;<span class=\\"hljs-name\\">p</span>&gt;</span>Some text<span class=\\"hljs-tag\\">&lt;/<span class=\\"hljs-name\\">p</span>&gt;</span>\\n            <span class=\\"hljs-tag\\">&lt;/<span class=\\"hljs-name\\">div</span>&gt;</span>\\n        <span class=\\"hljs-tag\\">&lt;/<span class=\\"hljs-name\\">Loader</span>&gt;</span></span>\\n    );\\n}</code></pre>\\n<h3 id=\\"fig-2---compiled\\">Fig 2 - Compiled</h3>\\n<pre><code class=\\"hljs language-js\\"><span class=\\"hljs-meta\\">\\"use strict\\"</span>;\\n\\n<span class=\\"hljs-function\\"><span class=\\"hljs-keyword\\">function</span> <span class=\\"hljs-title\\">App</span>(<span class=\\"hljs-params\\"></span>) </span>{\\n    <span class=\\"hljs-keyword\\">return</span> React.createElement(\\n        Loader,\\n        { <span class=\\"hljs-attr\\">complete</span>: <span class=\\"hljs-literal\\">false</span> },\\n        React.createElement(\\n            <span class=\\"hljs-string\\">\\"ul\\"</span>,\\n            <span class=\\"hljs-literal\\">null</span>,\\n            React.createElement(<span class=\\"hljs-string\\">\\"li\\"</span>, <span class=\\"hljs-literal\\">null</span>, <span class=\\"hljs-string\\">\\"A\\"</span>),\\n            React.createElement(<span class=\\"hljs-string\\">\\"li\\"</span>, <span class=\\"hljs-literal\\">null</span>, <span class=\\"hljs-string\\">\\"B\\"</span>)\\n        ),\\n        React.createElement(\\n            <span class=\\"hljs-string\\">\\"div\\"</span>,\\n            <span class=\\"hljs-literal\\">null</span>,\\n            React.createElement(<span class=\\"hljs-string\\">\\"p\\"</span>, <span class=\\"hljs-literal\\">null</span>, <span class=\\"hljs-string\\">\\"Some text\\"</span>)\\n        )\\n    );\\n}</code></pre>\\n<p>This is a small example, but if there are alot of children, with complex logic of their own</p>\\n<h2 id=\\"solution\\">Solution</h2>\\n<p>For this example it was simple, return either the Loader or the children, but not both.</p>\\n<h3 id=\\"fig-3\\">Fig 3</h3>\\n<pre><code class=\\"hljs language-js\\"><span class=\\"hljs-function\\"><span class=\\"hljs-keyword\\">function</span> <span class=\\"hljs-title\\">App</span>(<span class=\\"hljs-params\\"></span>) </span>{\\n\\n    <span class=\\"hljs-keyword\\">if</span>(isComplete) {\\n        <span class=\\"hljs-keyword\\">return</span> <span class=\\"xml\\"><span class=\\"hljs-tag\\">&lt;<span class=\\"hljs-name\\">Loader</span> /&gt;</span></span>\\n    }\\n\\n    <span class=\\"hljs-keyword\\">return</span> (\\n        <span class=\\"xml\\"><span class=\\"hljs-tag\\">&lt;<span class=\\"hljs-name\\">div</span>&gt;</span>\\n            <span class=\\"hljs-tag\\">&lt;<span class=\\"hljs-name\\">ul</span>&gt;</span>\\n              <span class=\\"hljs-tag\\">&lt;<span class=\\"hljs-name\\">li</span>&gt;</span>A<span class=\\"hljs-tag\\">&lt;/<span class=\\"hljs-name\\">li</span>&gt;</span>\\n              <span class=\\"hljs-tag\\">&lt;<span class=\\"hljs-name\\">li</span>&gt;</span>B<span class=\\"hljs-tag\\">&lt;/<span class=\\"hljs-name\\">li</span>&gt;</span>\\n            <span class=\\"hljs-tag\\">&lt;/<span class=\\"hljs-name\\">ul</span>&gt;</span>\\n            <span class=\\"hljs-tag\\">&lt;<span class=\\"hljs-name\\">div</span>&gt;</span>\\n              <span class=\\"hljs-tag\\">&lt;<span class=\\"hljs-name\\">p</span>&gt;</span>Some text<span class=\\"hljs-tag\\">&lt;/<span class=\\"hljs-name\\">p</span>&gt;</span>\\n            <span class=\\"hljs-tag\\">&lt;/<span class=\\"hljs-name\\">div</span>&gt;</span>\\n        <span class=\\"hljs-tag\\">&lt;/<span class=\\"hljs-name\\">div</span>&gt;</span></span>\\n    );\\n}</code></pre>\\n<h3 id=\\"fig-4\\">Fig 4</h3>\\n<pre><code class=\\"hljs language-js\\"><span class=\\"hljs-meta\\">\\"use strict\\"</span>;\\n\\n<span class=\\"hljs-function\\"><span class=\\"hljs-keyword\\">function</span> <span class=\\"hljs-title\\">App</span>(<span class=\\"hljs-params\\"></span>) </span>{\\n\\n    <span class=\\"hljs-keyword\\">if</span> (isComplete) {\\n        <span class=\\"hljs-keyword\\">return</span> React.createElement(Loader, <span class=\\"hljs-literal\\">null</span>);\\n    }\\n\\n    <span class=\\"hljs-keyword\\">return</span> React.createElement(\\n        <span class=\\"hljs-string\\">\\"div\\"</span>,\\n        <span class=\\"hljs-literal\\">null</span>,\\n        React.createElement(\\n            <span class=\\"hljs-string\\">\\"ul\\"</span>,\\n            <span class=\\"hljs-literal\\">null</span>,\\n            React.createElement(<span class=\\"hljs-string\\">\\"li\\"</span>, <span class=\\"hljs-literal\\">null</span>, <span class=\\"hljs-string\\">\\"A\\"</span>),\\n            React.createElement(<span class=\\"hljs-string\\">\\"li\\"</span>, <span class=\\"hljs-literal\\">null</span>, <span class=\\"hljs-string\\">\\"B\\"</span>)\\n        ),\\n        React.createElement(\\n            <span class=\\"hljs-string\\">\\"div\\"</span>,\\n            <span class=\\"hljs-literal\\">null</span>,\\n            React.createElement(<span class=\\"hljs-string\\">\\"p\\"</span>, <span class=\\"hljs-literal\\">null</span>, <span class=\\"hljs-string\\">\\"Some text\\"</span>)\\n        )\\n    );\\n}</code></pre>\\n","showInResults":true,"tags":["react","javascript"]}')}}]);